lement river-contact-water@1 through the current development handoff. Public interface access-water: strict schema {mode:inspect|form-cup|fill|wet|inspect-cup|resume|cancel, target:string, container:string, project:string, quantityMl:integer>=0, x:number,y:number}; unused references empty, unused quantities/coordinates zero. References resolve exact persistent IDs, optionally one appropriate item:/object: prefix, never resource aliases. Targets may also identify an inspected river surface cell. Personal study: two rounds; no simulation time passes during implementation.\\nState and physical dependencies: use the authoritative river-terrain polygon, shared collision geometry and current water conditions. Add versioned finite surface-water compartments only on actual river cells: initially 10 litres per square metre of wetted area, representing a declared 1 cm withdrawable surface layer, not measured actor knowledge or an unlimited river supply. No automatic replenishment in this minimal version. Persist cell volume, withdrawals, provenance and contamination-unknown status. Inspection reports geometric access and estimated available volume, not potability. If authoritative river geometry does not establish a water surface, report unresolved access without creating one.\\nAccess: actor remains on supported non-water terrain; interaction segment to water or apparatus must be <=0.65, clear of solids, and not require entering water. Coordinate x=26 alone does not establish reach from (25,15). Inspection costs one round/0.2 energy and records actual bank/surface geometry and uncertainty. It neither moves the actor nor wets a remote specimen.\\nExecutable portable precursor: form-cup uses 0.5 kg of explicitly owned wet clay at a clear reachable work footprint, three stages of one round/0.5 energy each. Reject inadequate quantity before allocation; partition material precisely by mass. Persist a hand-formed open cup, 0.1 litre capacity, 0.03 m outer radius, 0.07 m height, clay provenance and remaining wall mass. This is fragile unfired clay, not ceramic. Declare model law: when holding water, lose 1 ml water and 0.1 g wall clay per round into an actual located spill containing clay sediment; at wall mass below 0.45 kg, collapse, spilling remaining water and retaining all clay as wet fragments. Carrying or dropping updates actual location and load; ordinary collision damage also applies. No insulation, sterilization or food-safety effects.\\nFill: reachable inspected river compartment plus actual accessible cup, positive quantityMl within free capacity and remaining source volume; one round/0.3 energy. Atomically debit source and credit cup, preserving source/time lineage. Wet: exact locally accessible specimen accepted by an existing material-test contract; one round/0.3 energy. Use 10 ml per 0.1 material unit as the initial versioned contact-water dose, rounded upward to whole ml. Withdraw either from a reachable inspected river compartment for immediate contact or from an explicit local cup. Transfer water into the specimen's tracked moisture and subsequent runoff/evaporation, not an unexplained deletion. Bind this operation to assay-woven-supports so its actual wet stage can consume this dose and proceed only with its own remaining paid work and local specimen. It supplies no pass certificate. No ingestion operation is introduced.\\nContracts: persist operation ID, owner, exact escrow IDs, paid stages, actual remaining work and completion flag. Insufficient energy/access pauses without charge. Resume executes only remaining stages; repeat starts a new fully costed operation. Cancellation, incompatible action or death cancels attended multi-round work and releases surviving escrow once at its actual location; never clone, delete or refund used material/effort. Completed cups and passive leakage persist independently. Concurrent withdrawals use atomic shared locks. Migration leaves existing waterless trials paused and existing objects unchanged; never backfill water or rewrite evidence. Record any reused resolver, escrow and wet-trial code separately from this new function.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Actual paid inspection or a performed wet comparison may establish previously unknown access or material behavior. Subscribe information-confirmed with interface access-water to the existing grounded-understanding source: only the acting observer, qualified new observed information, 0.8 transient amount, cap 1, eight-round duration, refresh repetition and 12-round cooldown; maintained gain 0.035 per eligible event with existing 0.0015 decay and the source's bounded saturation. Share deduplication with probe and material assays: the same access fact or wet-test result cannot pay twice. Repeated known filling, cup fabrication, requesting and learning receive no curiosity or mastery reward. No separate maintained satisfaction source is warranted merely for possessing water; no hydration, nutrition, health or protected mental-account changes are implied.\",\"visualReview\":\"Declare water-access-inspected, water-cup-progress, water-cup-completed, water-withdrawn, material-contact-wetted, water-spilled, water-cup-failed and water-operation-stopped for subscription validation, alongside existing information-confirmed. Render cups and work footprints at their shared physical coordinates, with visible fill level, wet clay condition, spills and failure remnants. Replay events include actor, source/cup/specimen IDs, location, before/after volumes and masses, paid energy, stage and remaining work. Inspection overlays distinguish observed reachable surface, blocked reach and uncertainty; they must not display a remote test as completed or water as potable.\",\"learning\":2}]}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"d59aff6c-06e2-4e42-9823-707e8c58a877","prompt_cache_retention":"